0 (type-level refactoring — no runtime cost, pure clarity gain)**\n\n### Step 6: Decision Documentation\n\n**Refactoring Applied:**\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: Replaced `results: unknown[]` with an explicit `QuoteResult { premium: number }` type and annotated the `.map` callback's return type.\n\n**Benefits:**\n- The public API now documents its actual output shape instead of hiding it behind `unknown[]`.\n- Restores compile-time type safety for consumers of `ScenarioResult`.\n- Zero runtime APP mass cost — pure intent-revealing improvement.\n\n**Rejected alternatives (documented per process):**\n- Extracting `count = items.length` inside `componentsBasePremium`: would add binding + assignment mass without meaningful clarity gain (`items.length` is already clear). Skipped.\n- Multi-block/per-type grouping logic: explicitly a *future test* (7 runes, separate blocks) — not implemented to avoid speculative generality (Rule 4: Fewest Elements).\n\n### Step 7: Completion Report\n\n```\nRefactoring Complete:\nRefactoring: Introduced explicit QuoteResult type; replaced `unknown[]` with `QuoteResult[]` (Rule 2 – Reveals Intent)\nMass Change: unchanged (type-level refactoring, no runtime cost)\nTests: All passing (4 passed | 28 todo)\n```"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-4/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 4\nRecent Green phase: componentsBasePremium now returns BLOCK_BASE only when exactly BLOCK_SIZE components, else count*COMPONENT_BASE. Note: multi-block grouping (e.g. 7 runes, or per-type blocks) is a future test — do not add yet.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim-office.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim-office.ts\nPassing tests: 4\nRecent Green phase: componentsBasePremium now returns BLOCK_BASE only when exactly BLOCK_SIZE components, else count*COMPONENT_BASE. Note: multi-block grouping (e.g. 7 runes, or per-type blocks) is a future test — do not add yet.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784906940185},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll analyze the current implementation and tests, then apply refactoring following the Simple Design Rules."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_017xoZWZra8JkjEz5fdeN7tD","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01WvFaLFaeHpGV2drgVjdEkJ","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim-office.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":248,"output":140,"cacheRead":9696,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10084,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784906940205,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-bff45e3d-a67c-40be-9329-2cd7708e4adf","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_017xoZWZra8JkjEz5fdeN7tD","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"const PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;\n\nconst COMPONENT_BASE = 25;\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_BASE = 60;\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n}\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ntype Step = QuoteStep;\n\nexport interface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nexport interface ScenarioResult {\n  results: unknown[];\n}\n\nconst componentsBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  if (items.length === BLOCK_SIZE) return BLOCK_BASE;\n  return items.length * COMPONENT_BASE;\n};\n\nconst quotePremium = (step: QuoteStep): number => {\n  const components = step.items.filter((i) => COMPONENT_TYPES.has(i.type));\n  const policyBase = componentsBasePremium(components);\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = policyBase * FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE;\n  return Math.ceil(policyBase + firstInsuranceSurcharge + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n\nexport const runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): ScenarioResult => {\n  const results = scenario.steps.map((step) => ({ premium: quotePremium(step) }));\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784906942327},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01WvFaLFaeHpGV2drgVjdEkJ","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { runScenario } from \"./claim-office.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"MHPCO Claim Office\", () => {\n  // --- Base premiums for main items (single item, no modifiers, newcomer 0 years) ---\n  // Note: a single-item quote for a newcomer includes +10% first-insurance and +5 fee.\n  // We isolate base-premium behaviour via the integration/edge tests below.\n\n  // --- Edge: empty item list ---\n  it(\"empty item list -> premium 5 G (only processing fee)\", () => {\n    const res = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [] }],\n    });\n    expect(res.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 5 });\n  });\n\n  // --- Component blocks (base premium examples) ---\n  it(\"2 runes -> 50 G base premium\", () => {\n    const res = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    // base 50 + first-insurance 10% (5) + fee 5 = 60\n    expect(res.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 60 });\n  });\n  it(\"3 runes -> 60 G base premium (block applies)\", () => {\n    const res = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    // block base 60 + first-insurance 10% (6) + fee 5 = 71\n    expect(res.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 71 });\n  });\n  it(\"4 runes -> 100 G base premium (no block; needs exactly 3)\", () => {\n    const res = runScenario({\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }, { type: \"rune\" }] }],\n    });\n    // no block: 4*25=100 + first-insurance 10 + fee 5 = 115\n    expect(res.results[0]).toEqual({ premium: 115 });\n  });\n  it.todo(\"7 runes -> 175 G base premium\");\n\n  // --- 'Alike' components ---\n  it.todo(\"2 runes + 1 moonstone -> 75 G base premium (no block: different types)\");\n  it.todo(\"3 runes + 3 moonstones -> 120 G base premium (two separate blocks)\");\n\n  // --- Modifier scope on multi-item policies ---\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword (100) + plain amulet (60) -> 210 G before further modifiers and fee\");\n\n  // --- Modifier thresholds ---\n  it.todo(\"customer with exactly 2 years -> loyalty discount applies\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with exactly enchantment 5 -> high-enchantment surcharge applies\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword with enchantment 5 -> both curse and high-enchantment surcharges apply\");\n  it.todo(\"sword with enchantment 4 -> no high-enchantment surcharge\");\n\n  // --- Integration examples ---\n  it.todo(\"newcomer with cursed sword (steel, ench 3) -> premium 165 G\");\n  it.todo(\"long-standing customer's second contract, cursed sword ench 7 -> premium 160 G\");\n\n  // --- Rounding ---\n  it.todo(\"premium yielding 197.5 G -> final premium 198 G (rounded up)\");\n  it.todo(\"payout yielding 350.5 G -> final payout 350 G (rounded down)\");\n\n  // --- Claim: standard reimbursement ---\n  it.todo(\"regular sword (steel, ench 3), damage 500 -> payout 400 (full minus deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"rune (value 250), damage 200 -> payout 100 (no special clause)\");\n\n  // --- Claim: high enchantment / dragon material ---\n  it.todo(\"steel sword, ench 9, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (50% then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon-material sword, ench 5, damage 800 -> payout 700 (full then deductible)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon-material sword, ench 9, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (50% rule wins)\");\n  it.todo(\"dragon-material sword, ench 8, damage 1000 -> payout 400 (high-ench clause then deductible)\");\n\n  // --- Deductible per damage event ---\n  it.todo(\"sword (500) and amulet (300) damaged -> payout 600 (deductible per item)\");\n\n  // --- Multiple items of same type ---\n  it.todo(\"policy with two swords -> insurance sum 2000, both swords damaged handled separately\");\n  it.todo(\"more sword damages than swords insured -> claim rejected (non-zero exit)\");\n\n  // --- Cap ---\n  it.todo(\"policy sword + amulet -> insurance sum 1600, cap 3200\");\n  it.todo(\"cursed sword -> cap 2000 (based on unmodified insurance value)\");\n  it.todo(\"policy sword + 3 runes block -> insurance sum 1750\");\n  it.todo(\"cap exhaustion: two 1500 claims on sword -> 1400 then 600, remaining 0\");\n\n  // --- Error cases ---\n  it.todo(\"unknown item type in quote -> CLI exits non-zero, error to stderr\");\n  it.todo(\"claim references item not in policy -> CLI exits non-zero\");\n  it.todo(\"claim damage amount -200 -> CLI exits non-zero\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784906942327},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Running the tests to verify everything passes.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_011UMQcFNDco8ibodT1XA9nh","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_15-24-24_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_opus-4-8-4 && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":2889,"output":147,"cacheRead":96