ing 1 + inv 2 + inv 2(*) + inv 2(+) = 7\nreturn Math.ceil(...)                     inv 2 + inv 2+2 = 6\n```\n`quotePremium` body ≈ **29** (was ~57). The extracted helpers carry the loop/conditional mass but each now has a clear name and single responsibility.\n\n### Step 6: Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- **Naming (Rule 2)**: Extracted `mainItemsBasePremium` and `curseSurcharge` as named helpers, mirroring the existing `componentsBasePremium`. The main-items pricing path now reads symmetrically with the components path instead of hiding logic in anonymous inline reduces.\n- **Duplication (Rule 3)**: The two `mainItems.reduce(... MAIN_ITEM_BASE[i.type] ...)` expressions both re-encoded \"look up base premium by item type.\" That knowledge is now localized in the two dedicated helpers.\n- **Fewest elements (Rule 4)**: Collapsed the intermediate `componentsBase`, `mainBase`, and `firstInsuranceSurcharge` bindings into the composed `policyBase`/`surcharges` expressions, reducing scattered scalar bindings.\n\nBenefits: `quotePremium` now reads as a clear pricing pipeline (base → surcharges → ceil with fee), each cost component is a self-describing function, and mass in the top-level function dropped substantially.\n\n### Step 7: Report\n\n**Refactoring Complete:**\n- **Refactoring**: Extracted `mainItemsBasePremium` and `curseSurcharge` helpers; simplified `quotePremium` into a base + surcharges pipeline.\n- **Mass Change**: `quotePremium` body ≈ 57 → 29 (loop/conditional mass relocated into named helpers).\n- **Tests**: All 8 passing (24 todo)."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":6774,"output":803,"cacheRead":9696,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":17273,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784907152397,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-2d681c3a-31cb-4e09-aa48-acec63762f61","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":21676,"output":3782,"cacheRead":48942,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":17273,"turns":5},"model":"requesty/vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784907163563},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_014xWbSATgo15c4KNWiA81Gf","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -4; echo ---; cat src/claim-office.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":2222,"output":78,"cacheRead":39065,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":41365,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784907163564,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-1247b031-065f-4a23-b28b-3051af188506","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_014xWbSATgo15c4KNWiA81Gf","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"      Tests  8 passed | 24 todo (32)\n   Start at  15:32:45\n   Duration  163ms (transform 27ms, setup 0ms, collect 25ms, tests 3ms, environment 0ms, prepare 45ms)\n\n---\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE = 0.1;\n\nconst COMPONENT_BASE = 25;\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_BASE = 60;\n\nconst COMPONENT_TYPES = new Set([\"rune\", \"moonstone\"]);\n\nconst MAIN_ITEM_BASE: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst CURSE_RATE = 0.5;\n\ninterface Item {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\ninterface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\ntype Step = QuoteStep;\n\nexport interface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ScenarioResult {\n  results: QuoteResult[];\n}\n\nconst countByType = (items: Item[]): Map<string, number> => {\n  const counts = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items) {\n    counts.set(item.type, (counts.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return counts;\n};\n\nconst blockBasePremium = (count: number): number =>\n  count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_BASE : count * COMPONENT_BASE;\n\nconst componentsBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const count of countByType(items).values()) {\n    total += blockBasePremium(count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n\nconst mainItemsBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, i) => sum + MAIN_ITEM_BASE[i.type], 0);\n\nconst curseSurcharge = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, i) => sum + (i.cursed ? MAIN_ITEM_BASE[i.type] * CURSE_RATE : 0), 0);\n\nconst quotePremium = (step: QuoteStep): number => {\n  const components = step.items.filter((i) => COMPONENT_TYPES.has(i.type));\n  const mainItems = step.items.filter((i) => i.type in MAIN_ITEM_BASE);\n\n  const policyBase = componentsBasePremium(components) + mainItemsBasePremium(mainItems);\n  const surcharges = curseSurcharge(mainItems) + policyBase * FIRST_INSURANCE_RATE;\n\n  return Math.ceil(policyBase + surcharges + PROCESSING_FEE);\n};\n\nexport const runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): ScenarioResult => {\n  const results = scenario.steps.map((step): QuoteResult => ({ premium: quotePremium(step) }));\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784907166155},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The refactor correctly consolidated first-insurance into surcharges since it applies to every quote unconditionally. Now I'm checking test 9, which validates that a customer with exactly 2 years of tenure qualifies for the 20% loyalty discount on the policy base.\n\nFor a 2-year customer with a single sword: the base is 100, loyalty discount brings it to 80, first-insurance adds 10, and the fee adds 5, totaling 95. Since this is their first quote, the follow-up contract discount doesn't apply—only the loyalty discount kicks in.","thinkingSignature":"reasoni